<section class="text-size-3">
  <h2>Page object pattern</h2>

  <p class="fragment" data-fragment-index="1">
    Page objects abstract away the technical interactions from the decision code
  </p>


  <!--
  "divide business-oriented decisions, workflows and technical interactions into separate layers."


  |  test layer   |  worfklow component        | technical interaction layer |
  |  - decisions  |  - manipulate page ojects  | -                           |
  |               |                            |



business decision layer:     | test 1 | test 2 | test 3 | ...                  |
worflow layer:               | worflow component 1 | worflow component 2 | ... |
technical interaction layer: | page object 1 | page object 2 | ... | Api client | Api client | ...| 
application:                 | UI                                  | API       |                   |

maybe mermaid's block diagram can help, or simply flex boxes...
-->

  <div class="flex-row fragment" data-fragment-index="2">

    <table class="mt-100" style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 1.2rem; width: 500px;">
      <tr>
        <td class="bold" style="text-align: center;  vertical-align: middle;">
          Business decision layer</td>
        <td style="padding: 1.5em .5em;">
          <div class="flex-row justify-content--flex-start gap-15">
            <div class="rectangle no-wrap"
              data-arrow="->page-object-1:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'}">
              <u>Test 1:</u><br> Verify login
            </div>
            <div class="rectangle no-wrap fragment" style="border-style: dashed;"
              data-arrow="->page-object-1:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top','dash':true,'color':'gray'};->page-object-2:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top','dash':true,'color':'gray'}"
              data-fragment-index="5">
              <u>Test 2:</u><br> Verify add to basket
            </div>
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="box" style="border-left: none; border-right: none;">
        <td class="bold" style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.3rem; vertical-align: middle;">
          Interaction layer</td>
        <td style="padding: 1.5em .5em; text-align: center;">
          <div class="flex-row gap-15" style="justify-content: center;">
            <div class="rectangle" id="page-object-1"
              data-arrow="->web-page:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'}">
              loginPage</div>
            <div class="rectangle fragment" id="page-object-2" style="border-style: dashed;"
              data-arrow="->web-page:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top','dash':true,'color':'gray'}"
              data-fragment-index="5">
              productPage
            </div>
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="bold" style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.3rem; vertical-align: middle;">
          Application</td>
        <td style="padding: 1.5em .5em; text-align: center;">
          <img src="img/flaticon_com__webpage_5681787_cropped.png" width="105" style="margin: 0;" id="web-page">
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <div style="font-size:80%">


      <if-pw>
        <pre class="fragment" data-fragment-index="3"><code class="typescript">
          await page                                  //
            .locator('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle') // this is about HTML
            .click()                                  // 
        </code></pre>
        <pre class="fragment" data-fragment-index="4"><code class="typescript">
          await cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();    // this is about the
                                                      // application
        </code></pre>
      </if-pw>


      <if-cy>
        <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cy.get('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle').click()  // this is about HTML
    </code></pre>
        <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();               // this is about the
                                                       // application
    </code></pre>
      </if-cy>

    </div>

  </div>



  <p class="mt-150 fragment">
    Tests with Page Objects are <strong>easier to read</strong> and
    <strong>easier to maintain</strong>
  </p>


</section>